## THE PROPERTY (every behaviour: the cells that hold it, three shapes of its subject that the cells do NOT use, and each one covered or named)
**(A) RD-1016.** *settings.js defines escapeHtml once; at the five validation sinks (the suggestion, the message, the suggestions, the saved id and the quick question message) an array holding markup and an object whose text form is markup are written as text (no element, no attribute); a string is written exactly as before; a number is its digits; null, undefined, 0, false and the empty string write nothing, as before.* **Cells:** E1 (one definition), E2 (an array), E3 (an object with a text form), E4 (a string), E5 (the scalars), A1 to A5 (an array at each sink), O1 (an object with a text form at all five), C1 (control: a plain object, what JSON gives, at all five), K1 (control: an ordinary string at all five). **Shapes outside the primary one (an array at a sink), each stated:** (i) *the other callers of the function in the file* (the 42 occurrences of `escapeHtml(` in the file at BASE, counted by `/usr/bin/grep -o -F 'escapeHtml(' | wc -l`, are the 2 definitions, the 5 sinks and 35 others: names, e-mails, error messages, a label, the toast): the function is global to the file, so each now escapes a non-string it used to write raw; **no cell calls those sites with a non-string** (named limit: a site that passed a non-string on purpose to get markup would change; the drafter read the argument expressions in the `grep -n` listing at BASE and none is a value built to carry markup, by reading that listing only, not by a program and not by a run); (ii) *a non-string whose text conversion throws* (an object whose `toString` throws): `String(...)` throws as it did before the change; **named limit, no cell**; (iii) *the other two scripts' functions* (`index.js` line 113 reads the text back through an element; `first-run-setup.js` line 2946 stringifies and replaces): **not changed and not read by a cell here**; a named limit (RD-1014 and its siblings). Further: the five sinks are the ones the ticket names; the other 11 HTML write sites of `settings.js` are RD-1014's.
**(B) RD-1015.** *At the eight number cells of four exports (the sheets cell of the job history export and of the all-tabs export, the pages and size cells of the scanning export, the sheets and cost cells of the anomalies rows of the anomalies export and of the all-tabs export), a value that csvCell would prefix (a formula) is written through csvCell, as text with a visible quote, and every other value is written byte for byte as before; zero is written as 0; no other cell of any export changes.* **Cells:** U1 (the helper on formula-shaped values), U2 (the helper on every other value, including 0, '', null, a dash, a currency text, `1,234` and a value with a quote), U3 (a leading space, a new line and two look-alikes are still written as before: part (2) not decided), X1 and X2 (the job history sheets cell of a print and of a scan job), X3 (the all-tabs job section), X4 and X5 (the scanning pages and size cells), X6 and X7 (the anomalies sheets and cost cells, in the anomalies export and in the all-tabs export), K1 to K3 (controls: an ordinary scanning row, an ordinary anomalies row, zero sheets), C1 (the helper is called at the eight cells: one definition and eight calls), C2 (defined once, and csvCell still once). **Shapes outside the tested one (a formula name in a cell), each stated:** (i) *a value beginning with a space, a new line or a look-alike character*: NOT neutralised, **pinned by U3 as "as before", part (2) of the ticket, named**; (ii) *a negative amount with a currency sign in these cells* (`-$1.20`): csvCell prefixes it, so it opens as text with a visible quote (ticket part (3), which the review accepted); covered by U1, the drafter found no writer of one in these cells by reading (the anomalies cost is written as `$` then the number; not an exhaustive search); (iii) *a thousands comma or a quote in a non-formula value* (`1,234`): written raw as before, so a row can gain a column: **named limit, finding 6, U2 pins it unchanged**. Further named limits: the code-summed counters and the sample-data writers (finding 3); `cost` of the job rows; the audit log export on the server side (`backend/server.js`, the ticket names it and it is not this lane's); a spreadsheet's reading of the prefixed cell (UNMEASURED: no spreadsheet).
**(C)** Nothing is built for RD-1014's sites, the leading-space and look-alike cases, the thousands-comma row split, or a server-side export. **Tested shapes:** the lane's runs (red-first at BASE in both shapes, green in both, each mutation red on exactly its cells), the neighbours, the whole suite once in the Linux shape, the plain verify. **Shapes outside, said so:** a real browser, a hosted instance, a real Linux file system (none is used), a spreadsheet.

