At about 70% context start no new part; at about 75% stop at a safe boundary (a commit made or not started, files whole, every process you started stopped by pid, bands free, the lock released or your ticket named) and write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-27_B2143_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps) with last line `HANDOVER B2143: next <part> <step> | done <parts>`, and end STATUS with the same line. Parts: read, trees, lane, commits, linux-update, plain, cq, push. **Size (Q-1):** the seat's heavy steps are the two whole-suite runs (B2133's drafter measured 1313 seconds for the whole suite in the Linux shape at its load; this kit's are PREDICTED the same) and the lane (the dry run's 54 judge calls are small cells; its jest time is PREDICTED a few minutes); **add the lock queue's wait behind the live data-erasure seat to the clock.** If the band is reached before step 5, the commits already made are not pushed (HARD STOP).

